Z||000025||Urchin||08-21-2001||09:22 PM||||<BR>[/b][/QUOTE]<BR>Never quitting the habit    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> we just have too many toys right now but I may get another Fiero later.  Right now I'm enjoying the new jet boat.  Beck still has hers but then again, she does have the nicer car of the two. . .<P>[/B][/QUOTE]<P>Good to hear.  I was afraid us Londoners were going to start dropping in numbers.  It's bad enough that I have to get rid of mine.  I should have another and better one next summer though.  Until then I guess I'll just have to admire them from the outside rather than the drivers seat.<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000026||Dave Gunsul||08-21-2001||09:43 PM||||The colors name is Orbit orange. It's a 1970 GTO color and as far as i've been able to tell it was only available on the GTO in 1970. 1970 was the only year it was available but what i'm not sure of is weather it was available on the Firebird or not.<P>Moocow: You shouldn't make that offer to me because I love to test drive anything!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>I don't know how equal they'd be though depends on what you've done to the 3.4.<P>Bazooka: the engine has only two hundred and<BR>some odd miles on it so it will be some time before it's stepped on at all. I can tell you that with all the mods that have been done to it the car is, even in my babbying it<BR>driving style, MUCH stronger than it was.<P>Sqoach: Orbit orange is a very yellowish orange color. In the daytime it looks more yellow and as the sunsets it turns more and more orange. If Tigger and I were to park next to each other his would be a lot darker than mine.<BR>The upper plenum is jet hot coated and then polished.<P>BTW guys I forgot to mention a couple-a things in my list of mods: <BR>ASP pulley.<BR>Kosei K1 lightweight racing wheels. (13IB's)<BR>Kirkey lightweight racing seat. (pass. seat has been removed as well as the spare, jack,<BR>cruise control,and air conditioning.)<P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver<P>[This message has been edited by Dave Gunsul (edited 08-21-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by Dave Gunsul (edited 08-21-2001).]||||reg||1
