Z||000034||firstfiero||08-22-2001||09:54 AM||||    How much and how hard was it to install that momo seat? Damn good looking car!<P>------------------<BR><BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/firstfiero.gif"> ||||reg||14
Z||000035||Dave Gunsul||08-22-2001||02:52 PM||||Haze: since Oreif beat me to it you know already that the tips are Ocelot but I must caution you about them. The tips are made from, as Oreif calls them soft chrome, I call<BR>them cheap chrome, this means that they will rust very easily and quickly if exposed to any rain or salt so be aware that if yuo put them on a car that sees this kind of weather they may rust quickly. This isn't a problem for me since my car doesn't see bad weather<BR>anymore.<P>Oreif: I, myself, will go if it rains or not but the car will only go if there's no rain.<P>First Fiero: The seat isn't a Momo seat it's a Kirkey. Mounting it wasn't hard at all since the original Fiero seat brackets were<BR>mounted on the bottom. Also: thanks very much for the compliment. Your car looks good in your sig. too!<P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||1
